cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use whatleaks or its benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "whatleaks: see what an app you run sends home, and what it still sends after you opt out"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ranjan
    given-names: Devansh
repository-code: "https://github.com/devanshranjan10/whatleaks"
url: "https://whatleaks.me"
abstract: >-
  whatleaks runs a command through a local, single-run proxy and reports where its traffic went,
  which fields each payload carried, whether any of it identifies the machine or user, and what is
  still sent after opting out of telemetry. Its benchmark measures how often HTTP(S) capture tools
  silently miss what a program sends, against exact ground truth: 46 lab scenarios (594 attempts)
  on macOS and 43 (567) on Linux, plus real tools checked against their own debug output.
keywords:
  - telemetry
  - privacy
  - opt-out
  - DO_NOT_TRACK
  - network capture
  - HTTPS proxy
  - benchmark
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-24"
